  "body": "Part of the deployment-architecture epic (design: PR #5764, `doc/2026-11-04_deployment-architecture-services-layer.md` §3–§4).\n\nBuild the `deploy` package in the code flake:\n\n- A `deployTargets` flake output: the merged registry of service definitions (this repo's + the forks', imported via their flake outputs). Each definition is the §3 option set (package, entryPoint, args, environment, secrets-by-name, user, ports, restart, healthCheck, targets).\n- The `deploy` CLI with `list`, `deploy <target>`, `deploy <target> rollback`, `deploy <target> status`, `--dry-run`.\n- systemd activation (laptop class): per-service nix profile at `/nix/var/nix/profiles/per-service/<name>`; activation = install generation into the profile, write the rendered unit pointing at the profile link, daemon-reload, restart only that unit, run the health check; any failure flips the profile back and restarts on the previous generation.\n- Generation log per target (generation id, source rev, timestamp, actor), retained ≥2 generations.\n- launchd rendering may land as a stub behind the same definition shape in v1; systemd + status/rollback must be real.\n\nAcceptance: on the laptop, a harmless test service (or the M1 route-proxy) deploys, serves, rolls back, and reports status end-to-end with no `nixos-rebuild` and no home-manager activation in the loop; `deploy list` enumerates the registry; a deliberately broken generation fails its health check and auto-flips back.\n\nOut of scope: Cloudflare/container target classes (separate issues), migrating production services beyond the acceptance test (M1–M4 issues).\n",
